sections.s5b_flow:
```
  ═══ @FunctionalInterface: NOT MANDATORY BUT RECOMMENDED ═══

  WITHOUT annotation:
    interface FeeCalculator { BigDecimal calculate(Trade t); }
    // Works with lambdas (Recommended) 
    // BUT: adding 2nd abstract method → no compile error at interface
    // Error appears at every lambda usage site → hard to trace!

  WITH annotation:
    @FunctionalInterface
    interface FeeCalculator { BigDecimal calculate(Trade t); }
    // Works with lambdas (Recommended) 
    // Adding 2nd abstract method → COMPILE ERROR right at the interface!
    // Bug caught at SOURCE, not at usage site.

  ═══ COMPOSITION VIA DEFAULT METHODS ═══

  FeeCalculator.percentageFee(0.001)
    │ calculate = trade → amount × 0.001
    │
    .withMinimum(20)                          ← default method
    │ wraps: trade → { fee = inner.calculate(trade); return max(fee, 20); }
    │
    .withMaximum(2500)                        ← default method
    │ wraps: trade → { fee = inner.calculate(trade); return min(fee, 2500); }
    │
    .withDiscount(0.10)                       ← default method
      wraps: trade → { fee = inner.calculate(trade); return fee × 0.90; }

  Final composed.calculate(trade):
    Outermost (discount) → calls middle (max) → calls inner (min) → calls base (percentage)
    Like Russian nesting dolls — each layer adds a rule!

  ═══ CAN EXTEND ANOTHER INTERFACE ═══

  interface Describable { String describe(); }  // 1 abstract

  @FunctionalInterface
  interface TradeAction extends Describable {
      void execute();                            // + describe() = 2 abstract → ERROR!
      default String describe() { return ""; }   // override as default → 1 abstract (Recommended) 
  }
```
